{
  "summary": "A PowerShell command using Invoke-Command to execute a hidden nested PowerShell process on a remote computer, a pattern commonly associated with lateral movement and remote code execution.",
  "is_malicious": "Likely",
  "explain": "This command uses Invoke-Command for remote execution combined with nested PowerShell launching (-nop -w hidden -c). The -w hidden flag hides the window from the user, and the nested powershell.exe process is a common technique used for both legitimate remote administration and malicious lateral movement. The pattern (remote targeting + hidden window + nested execution) is frequently observed in offensive tools and post-exploitation frameworks, making it highly suspicious even though Invoke-Command itself is a legitimate management cmdlet.",
  "tag": "LATERAL_MOVEMENT",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "code": "Invoke-Command -ComputerName <target> -ScriptBlock { ... }",
      "code_explain": "Invoke-Command is a legitimate PowerShell Remoting cmdlet (WinRM/PSRemoting) that allows executing scripts on remote computers. This is commonly exploited by attackers for lateral movement when valid credentials or access are available.",
      "tag": "REMOTE_COMMAND_EXECUTION"
    },
    {
      "code": "powershell -nop -w hidden -c <command>",
      "code_explain": "Launches a nested PowerShell process with: -nop (no profile, faster/stealthier), -w hidden (hidden window - evades user visibility), -c (command). This nested execution pattern inside a remote session is a hallmark of offensive operations and is used to bypass logging or execution restrictions.",
      "tag": "DEFENSE_EVASION"
    },
    {
      "code": "-w hidden",
      "code_explain": "The -w hidden parameter runs the PowerShell window in a hidden state, preventing the user from seeing command execution. This is a common defense evasion technique used to hide malicious activity from end users.",
      "tag": "DEFENSE_EVASION"
    },
    {
      "code": "-nop",
      "code_explain": "The -nop (NoProfile) flag prevents loading the user profile, which speeds up execution and reduces logging artifacts. This is frequently used in attack scripts to minimize detection surface.",
      "tag": "DEFENSE_EVASION"
    }
  ]
}
```

